SUMMARY:Embossed Stories: Mexican Repujado & Visual Language
DESCRIPTION:How can an object tell a story without words?Explore repujado
 \, a traditional Mexican metal-embossing technique\, through an artistic
  exploration of symbols\, visual language\, and storytelling.In this han
 ds-on workshop\, participants will create an original embossed metal pie
 ce inspired by a meaningful symbol\, place\, object\, personal story\, o
 r idea. Working with line\, pattern\, texture\, relief\, and form\, part
 icipants will discover how decorative elements can communicate ideas\, e
 motions\, identity\, and a sense of place.Drawing inspiration from Mexic
 an folk-art traditions and decorative arts\, the work\nhttps://www.princ
 eton.edu/events/2026/embossed-stories-mexican-repujado-visual-language
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/embossed-stories-mexican-repuja
 do-visual-language
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
