SUMMARY:Seuls en Scène 2026 presents Nom by Constance Debré
DESCRIPTION:Hugues Jourdain and Victoria Quesnel have crafted a captivati
 ng production based on the novel\, Nom\, written by Constance Debré. In
  her third book\, Debré pursues her relentless quest for freedom\, char
 ting a new course in her struggle: how to love better? She casts off the
  "corpses" haunting her life and abandons almost everything—family\, m
 arriage\, career—even contemplating the abolition of her lineage and h
 er family name. On a bare stage\, where only the power of words resonate
 s\, Victoria Quesnel—whose work in Julien Gosselin’s productions has
  drawn acclaim—makes this raw voice her own\, immersin\nhttps://www.pr
 inceton.edu/events/2026/seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-nom-constance-debre
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-no
 m-constance-debre
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
