SUMMARY:Seuls en Scène 2026 presents Barbara (par Barbara) by Marie-Soph
 ie Ferdane & Emmanuel Noblet
DESCRIPTION:This musical show is conceived as a contemporary radio broadc
 ast\, blending interviews\, archival material\, and previously unseen lo
 ve letters from the well-know French singer Barbara (1930-1997). Set in 
 a studio space with all-white floor and walls\, there is no physical pre
 sence of the incomparable singer—yet hers is the only voice you will h
 ear. Every word spoken is authentic and reflects the singer's freedom of
  expression\, her cheerfulness\, and her love for her craft as a "woman 
 who sings."Starring celebrated stage French actress Marie-Sophie Ferdane
  who makes her Seuls en Scène debut. "With \nhttps://www.princeton.edu/
 events/2026/seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-barbara-par-barbara-marie-sophi
 e-ferdane-emmanuel-noblet-0
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-ba
 rbara-par-barbara-marie-sophie-ferdane-emmanuel-noblet-0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
