SUMMARY:Responsible AI: Getting Set Up — Environments\, Tools\, and Avo
 iding Lock-In
DESCRIPTION:In this session\, we'll cover how to set up a research comput
 ing environment using VS Code\, Claude Code\, and other agentic coding t
 ools. We'll also work through the habits that outlast any single tool: k
 eeping an engineering mindset that avoids vendor lock-in\, staying in yo
 ur own environment rather than copy-pasting between a chat window and yo
 ur terminal\, and knowing when to follow a tutorial and when to ask an A
 I assistant for help. Participants will come away with a working\, flexi
 ble AI coding environment ready for the rest of the series\, and a set o
 f habits for evaluating tools and asking g\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/ev
 ents/2026/responsible-ai-getting-set-environments-tools-and-avoiding-loc
 k
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/responsible-ai-getting-set-envi
 ronments-tools-and-avoiding-lock
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
