SUMMARY:Perfume's Cultural Currents: A Selection of Historical Moments (a
 nd Smells)
DESCRIPTION:Just like works of visual art\, fashion\, or architecture\, f
 ragrance can be interpreted as material culture with specific historical
  contexts and enduring influence. In this multi-sensory program\, an ill
 ustrated lecture by fragrance historian Jessica Murphy will highlight ke
 y moments from perfumery’s long past while we sample a selection of re
 lated fragrant materials. How long have people been blending and using a
 romatic mixtures\, and why did they start doing it? How did France becom
 e known as the center of Western perfumery? What made some perfumes “m
 odern” in the late nineteenth century? After\nhttps://www.princeton.ed
 u/events/2026/perfumes-cultural-currents-selection-historical-moments-an
 d-smells
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/perfumes-cultural-currents-sele
 ction-historical-moments-and-smells
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
