SUMMARY:Seuls en Scène 2026 presents L’Événement by Annie Ernaux
DESCRIPTION:In L’événement\, Annie Ernaux (winner of the 2022 Nobel P
 rize in Literature) recounts—in detail and with the perspective gained
  over several decades—three months of her life between October 1963 an
 d January 1964: the three months spanning the time she discovered she wa
 s pregnant to the days following her abortion. During these three months
 \, her resolve clashed with the prejudices\, moral codes\, and violence 
 of a world shaped by male domination. Confronted by an abortionist\, she
  describes how she herself felt being born as a woman. The necessity of 
 her narrative serves to dispel only one form of \nhttps://www.princeton.
 edu/events/2026/seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-levenement-annie-ernaux
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/seuls-en-scene-2026-presents-le
 venement-annie-ernaux
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
