SUMMARY:The Keeper of My Kin\, Ada Ferrer
DESCRIPTION:A book reading and conversation from Pulitzer Prize–winning
  author Ada Ferrer on her latest memoir. A memoir about migration\, sepa
 ration\, and the love of one family forcing its way through the fissures
  of history. Professor Ferrer’s Pulitzer Prize-winning book Cuba: An A
 merican History (Scribner\, 2021) is a sweeping history of more than fiv
 e hundred years of Cuban history\, written in rousing and accessible pro
 se and based on more than thirty years of travel to and research on the 
 island. her first book\, Insurgent Cuba: Race\, Nation\, and Revolution\
 , 1868–1898\, was a history of the Cuban indepen\nhttps://www.princeto
 n.edu/events/2026/keeper-my-kin-ada-ferrer
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/keeper-my-kin-ada-ferrer
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
