SUMMARY:iASpace — Interaural Space
DESCRIPTION:iASpace is where sound\, bodies\, and presence come together\
 ; an experiment in collective attention. It is an invitation to what is 
 possible when listening is treated as a public resource\, and when a spa
 ce is dedicated to holding opacity rather than resolution. For seven day
 s\, the CoLab is transformed into a public space to stay\, listen\, retu
 rn\, and experience sound together.Schedule of Live Sound Works:9/29 at 
 5 PM — Sound performance with Leo Chang10/1 at 6 PM — Somatic Resona
 nce: Sound & Reiki workshop with Nanse & Bryce10/3 at 2 PM — Synth You
 th workshop with Sydney Spann10/4 at 11 AM — Dron\nhttps://www.princet
 on.edu/events/2026/iaspace-interaural-space-5
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/iaspace-interaural-space-5
