SUMMARY:HMEI Faculty Seminar: "How to Sink a Megacity: A Histoy of Water\
 , Land\, and Environmental Change in Mexico City" by Vera Candiani
DESCRIPTION:Vera Candiani\, Associate Professor of History\, will present
  “How to Sink a Megacity: A History of Water\, Land\, and Environmenta
 l Change in Mexico City” Join us in the Briger Hall Auditorium\, 11 Iv
 y Lane\, or stream it live. Candiani is the second speaker in the Fall 2
 026 HMEI Faculty Seminar Series. Modern Mexico City’s chronic flooding
 \, aquifer depletion\, and land subsidence are the cumulative result of 
 five centuries during which land speculators\, financiers\, state engine
 ers\, and political authorities transformed a lake basin into a megacity
