SUMMARY:Introduction to Lidar data
DESCRIPTION:Light Detection and Ranging (Lidar) data is a different kind 
 of remote sensing data that will allow the user to visualize\, analyze\,
  and extract a digital elevation model (DEM)\, slope and aspect\, height
  of trees\, 3D building views\, etc. In the United States\, the U.S. Geo
 logical Survey is collecting high-resolution Lidar data and making them 
 accessible to the public. In this class\, students will learn how to dow
 nload Lidar data and then visualize and analyze it\, and extract and cre
 ate DEMs and 3D building data.\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/in
 troduction-lidar-data
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/introduction-lidar-data
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
